Purpose of every article
Create trust and topical authority to the brand by educating and informing the audience. The article will focus on one single topic/problem audience has and go deep into the topic with our expertise. Content should help readers make informed decisions by providing accurate, practical, and technically sound information.
The objective is not to sell products. The objective is to become a trusted source of knowledge.

How Claude should think before writing
First analyze the topic, then look at the references in the internet for similar topics/white papers/case studies, gather information, relevance and then know the content gap, content gap can be also understood by listening to reddit queries and cross checking them in open web, linkedin or social channels if content exists for it. Then you can analyse the knowledge base of ours and get relevant information.
Every article should begin by understanding:
Who is the audience?
What problem or question are they trying to solve?
What level of technical knowledge should be assumed?
What search intent is being addressed?
What unique perspective can Luxury Concept contribute?
What practical value will the reader gain?

Content Objectives
Every article should achieve at least one of the following:
Educate
Explain
Clarify
Compare
Solve
Correct misconceptions
Provide decision-making guidance
Demonstrate expertise

Article Structure

Most educational articles should follow this flow:

Clear title
Executive summary
Introduction
Context
Main explanation
Supporting examples
Common misconceptions
Practical recommendations
Key takeaways
Frequently Asked Questions
Related topics
Suggested internal links
Not every article must follow this exactly, but the structure should remain logical and easy to navigate.

Writing Principles
Explain and humanise.
Don't sound AI.
Should be readable.
Have B2B copywriting style.
Write like Ogilvy does, hook them.
Never use fillers or unwanted poetic phrases.
Short and scannable sentences.
Use of good sophisticated english.

SEO principles
Satisfy the search intent.
Satisfy search intent.
Cover the topic comprehensively.
Build semantic relevance.
Naturally include related terminology.
Use descriptive headings.
Use clear URL structure.
Suggest internal links.
Suggest metadata.
Include structured FAQs when appropriate.

GEO principles
Clear definitions
Short factual statements
Comparisons
Decision frameworks
Tables when appropriate
Lists only when they improve understanding
Question-and-answer sections
Concise summaries before detailed explanations

AEO principles
Every article should naturally address:
What
Why
How
When
Where
Who
Common misconceptions
Frequently asked questions

